3. Acknowledgements (no code copied)
================================================================================

- FFmpeg (https://ffmpeg.org). port/src/media/audio.rs decodes Apple IMA4
  (the standard IMA ADPCM algorithm and its public step and index tables). One
  behaviour of FFmpeg's adpcm_ima_qt decoder is reproduced so that the output
  matches `ffmpeg -f s16le` sample for sample: the running predictor is kept
  when a packet header repeats the step index and a predictor close to the
  current one. No FFmpeg code is included, and FFmpeg is not linked or shipped:
  xf-prep runs the user's own ffmpeg executable as a separate process.
- MultimediaWiki (https://wiki.multimedia.cx) "Apple RPZA" and "Cinepak", and
  T. Ferguson's "Cinepak (CVID) stream format": the format descriptions that
  port/src/media/rpza2.rs and port/src/media/cinepak2.rs were written from.
- mthcore/x-files-game (MIT): published research on the HDB (NeoPersist)
  format. No code or headers from it are included.

